  1. Introduction 

     NiceEd is a User-Editor for the TransAmiga BBS package of
     programs for the Amiga computer. Its purpose in life is to make
     it easy for the SysOp of a TransAmiga system to look at users
     status and to change it as he sees fit.  

  2. Invocation 

     NiceEd can be started either from a CLI/Shell prompt, or
     directly from an icon. One is provided for your convenience, but
     feel free to design a new.  If you make an especially good one,
     please mail it to me.  

     2.1 Arguments 

     When started from Workbench or from CLI/Shell without any
     arguments NiceEd assumes your users directory is BBS:Users. If
     you start NiceEd from a CLI/Shell you can specify the path to
     your users-directory as the first and only argument on the
     command line.  Tooltypes is not supported yet, please mail me
     source showing how to do it "The Right Way".  

  3. Use 

     After a few seconds of disk-scanning the program will open a
     window (on your default public screen I hope) showing you the
     first user found.  You will see gadgets for all the users
     attributes on your BBS, and you will see some gadgets you can
     use for actually doing things with the program. Oh, yeah, right
     - there's a small little line mentioning my BBS.  Sorry, folks,
     I couldn't help it.  

     3.1 String and integer gadgets 

     The string gadgets are hopefully connected so that pressing
     return will make the cursor jump to the next gadget. Should work
     that way, anyhow.  

     3.2 Cycle gadgets 

     There are four of them and they "only" cycle to one other thing.
     I hate these gadgets when they can be in more that two
     positions, it makes it very confusing. Luckily there is a nice
     program called CycleToMenu that makes them roll down a menu,
     showing all the choices. Go get it! 

     3.3 Checkmark gadgets 

     These eight gadgets rule the "flags" of the user. I've been
     smart enough to use the numbers 1-8 for activating these from
     the keyboard...  

     3.4 Action gadgets 




  Page 3                 NiceEd User-confusion                  Page 3


     Yes, you read correctly - the program actually does something.  

        3.4.1 Choose User 

     This gadget makes a window containing a list of all the users
     pop up. Just doubleclick on the user you want to editor, and
     you're in for a treat.  

        3.4.2 Save User 

     Did yoy guess it yet? Right, it saves the (changed?) user to
     disk. Remeber to do this before moving on, if you want the
     changes you've made. If you just choose another user, the things
     you changed will be long gone.  

        3.4.3 New 

     Brings the first new user to be the one being edited. Pressing
     it again will take you to the next and so on. When there are no
     more new users, the gadget will crumble into a ghosted version
     and stop functioning until new users arrive at your BBS.  

        3.4.4 Normal (10) 

     Sets the current users access level to 10 and clears all his
     flags. Useful for validating new users, or degrading user with
     lots of access to normal.  

        3.4.5 < Previous 

     I hate spelling that word. Takes you one step up the list of
     users (remember to save changes to the current if any!). Beeps
     if you are at the top of the list.  

        3.4.6 > Next 

     Thats much easier to spell. Takes you one step down the list of
     users (remeber to save changes to the current if any!). Beeps if
     you are at the very bottom of the list.  

  4. Keyboard shortcuts 

     As all good programmers I tried to choose some nice shortcuts
     for you keyboard-maniacs out there. And isn't every one of us
     SysOp's a keyboard maniac? 

     Most of them is showed with the '_' standard underline, but some
     are hidden: 

     4.1 q, x 

     Ends the program, but ask first. Using the closewindow gadget
     just exits.  

     4.2 z 




  Page 4                 NiceEd User-confusion                  Page 4


     Same as pressing the zip-gadget.  

     4.3 Del 

     Deletes the current user, but is nice enough to ask you
     first...  

     4.4 Arrow-left <-, Arrow-right -> 

     Same as previous and next. Moves a user up/down.  

